<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Undoing a Transformation (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Let
\[ A = {@A@} \qquad\text{and}\qquad A^{-1} = {@Ai@}, \]
and take the vector
\[ \mathbf{x} = {@xx@}. \]</p>
<p>Compute \( \mathbf{y} = A\mathbf{x} \):</p>
<table style="border-collapse: collapse;">
  <tr>
    <td style="white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: middle;">
      \( \mathbf{y} = \)
    </td>
    <td style="white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: middle;">
      [[input:ans1]]
    </td>
<td style="white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: middle;">
      [[validation:ans1]]
    </td>
    <td style="white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: middle;">
      [[feedback:prt1]]
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
<p>Now use the inverse to recover \( \mathbf{x} \), i.e. compute \( A^{-1}\mathbf{y} \):</p>
<table style="border-collapse: collapse;">
  <tr>
    <td style="white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: middle;">
      \( A^{-1}\mathbf{y} = \)
    </td>
    <td style="white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: middle;">
      [[input:ans2]]
    </td>
<td style="white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: middle;">
      [[validation:ans2]]
    </td>
    <td style="white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: middle;">
      [[feedback:prt2]]
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Multiply \(A\) by \(\mathbf{x}\), taking each row of \(A\) against the column \(\mathbf{x}\):</p>
\[ \mathbf{y} = A\mathbf{x} = {@A@}{@xx@} = {@ta1@}. \]
<p>Applying the inverse undoes the transformation, returning the original vector:</p>
\[ A^{-1}\mathbf{y} = {@Ai@}{@ta1@} = {@ta2@} = \mathbf{x}. \]
<p>This is why \(A^{-1}A = I\): the inverse exactly reverses what \(A\) does.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
